{
 "fps": 30,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "h1",
   "part": "show",
   "start": 5.6,
   "end": 11.882,
   "text": "Good evening. You're tuned to First 100 Users: the things you saved about finding your first customers.",
   "quote": false,
   "source": null
  },
  {
   "id": "h2",
   "part": "show",
   "start": 12.262,
   "end": 15.061,
   "text": "First, an essay you kept on September twenty-third.",
   "quote": false,
   "source": null
  },
  {
   "id": "q1",
   "part": "show",
   "start": 15.511,
   "end": 19.798,
   "text": "You can't wait for users to come to you. You have to go out and get them.",
   "quote": true,
   "source": {
    "who": "Paul Graham",
    "title": "Do Things that Don't Scale",
    "site": "paulgraham.com",
    "saved": "Saved Sep 23"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "h3",
   "part": "show",
   "start": 20.248,
   "end": 25.357,
   "text": "Paul Graham. Same essay, on how the Collison brothers signed up Stripe's first users.",
   "quote": false,
   "source": null
  },
  {
   "id": "q2",
   "part": "show",
   "start": 25.807,
   "end": 27.686,
   "text": "Right then, give me your laptop.",
   "quote": true,
   "source": {
    "who": "Paul Graham, on Stripe",
    "title": "Do Things that Don't Scale",
    "site": "paulgraham.com",
    "saved": "Saved Sep 23"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "h4",
   "part": "show",
   "start": 28.136,
   "end": 32.595,
   "text": "And from the Superhuman story you saved that same afternoon, one question.",
   "quote": false,
   "source": null
  },
  {
   "id": "q3",
   "part": "show",
   "start": 33.045,
   "end": 35.716,
   "text": "How would you feel if you could no longer use the product?",
   "quote": true,
   "source": {
    "who": "Rahul Vohra, Superhuman",
    "title": "How Superhuman Built an Engine to Find Product Market Fit",
    "site": "First Round Review",
    "saved": "Saved Sep 23"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "h5",
   "part": "show",
   "start": 36.166,
   "end": 39.557,
   "text": "Three founders. One move. Nobody waited to be found.",
   "quote": false,
   "source": null
  },
  {
   "id": "x1",
   "part": "cross",
   "start": 43.437,
   "end": 48.761,
   "text": "Between First 100 Users and Product Stories, Ancher found something both shelves agree on.",
   "quote": false,
   "source": null
  },
  {
   "id": "x2",
   "part": "cross",
   "start": 49.141,
   "end": 55.092,
   "text": "You win people not by selling your big vision, but by the benefit one real person feels right now.",
   "quote": false,
   "source": null
  },
  {
   "id": "q4",
   "part": "cross",
   "start": 55.542,
   "end": 61.664,
   "text": "You should take extraordinary measures not just to acquire users, but also to make them happy.",
   "quote": true,
   "source": {
    "who": "Paul Graham",
    "title": "Do Things that Don't Scale",
    "site": "First 100 Users",
    "saved": "Saved Sep 23"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "q5",
   "part": "cross",
   "start": 62.114,
   "end": 68.214,
   "text": "When you frame ninety percent around how your recipient benefits, they are much more likely to take action.",
   "quote": true,
   "source": {
    "who": "Wes Kao",
    "title": "The Anatomy of a Great Cold Sales Pitch",
    "site": "Product Stories",
    "saved": "Saved Sep 22"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "x3",
   "part": "cross",
   "start": 68.664,
   "end": 70.253,
   "text": "Two shelves. One idea.",
   "quote": false,
   "source": null
  },
  {
   "id": "j1",
   "part": "latest",
   "start": 72.253,
   "end": 74.864,
   "text": "And the newest thing on your shelf, saved yesterday.",
   "quote": false,
   "source": null
  },
  {
   "id": "q6",
   "part": "latest",
   "start": 75.314,
   "end": 83.828,
   "text": "Most planning tools start from the entire internet and work down. This one starts from the handful of things someone already decided were worth keeping.",
   "quote": true,
   "source": {
    "who": "Farid Zeynalov",
    "title": "Curation-First Planning Tools",
    "site": "LinkedIn",
    "saved": "Saved Oct 1"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "j2",
   "part": "latest",
   "start": 84.278,
   "end": 85.741,
   "text": "Your library. On air.",
   "quote": false,
   "source": null
  }
 ],
